  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Division of labor",
      "items": [
        "LLM explains; the TypeScript kernel enumerates, evaluates, chooses",
        "solveUnified (Z3) serves the script/control plane; py is a historical oracle only",
        "Entries: async-collect.ts · state-cli.ts · replay.ts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Evidence & safety",
      "items": [
        "Render-layer source tags switch honestly on degradation; estimates never pose as realtime",
        "Session reads the user's own Chrome session (cookie names only); ReadGuard fails writes closed",
        "Booking/payment write paths must pass WriteGate first — nothing bookable today"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "State & async",
      "items": [
        "SQLite events/workflows are authoritative; JSON / Markdown are views",
        "Deep-planning hands off to a work order (ETA ≈1h), settled idempotently; tests use isolated stateRoots"
      ]
    }
  ]
